    (1316::bigint, jsonb_build_object(
      'queue_wait', 'The balcony bar is usually an easy daytime walk-in; student deals, live bands, salsa and Pride afterparties can create a busier Long Street door later. It is not known for a hard queer selection policy. Arrive before the headline set if you want a balcony rail rather than a squeeze near the bar.',
      'best_nights', 'Follow the event post: one night can mean salsa, another an alternative band, DJ set, student games or a Pride afterparty. Early hours suit pizza and people-watching over Long Street; after midnight the same room turns louder and looser. The programme, not Friday alone, decides whether it lands.',
      'crowd_mix', 'Students, Long Street regulars, live-music fans, tourists and queer-friendly party groups share the venue. Pride dates visibly increase the LGBTQ+ presence, but an ordinary night is broadly mixed rather than a gay club. The balcony draws visitors; themed events bring more Cape Town locals.',
      'dress_code', 'Casual city-night clothes are the norm: trainers, denim, band shirts and an easy party look. Salsa or Pride editions invite more effort, but no standing fashion code is published. Keep valuables close on Long Street and dress for a room that moves between pizza tables, balcony drinks and dancing.',
      'staff_inclusivity', 'Current guides present the venue as LGBTQ-friendly and active across varied communities, but the independent review sample is thin. One published diner review is positive; that is not enough for sweeping safety claims. Treat the event host and crowd on the night as more informative than the label alone.',
      'venue_classification', 'active_mixed_long_street_balcony_cafe_bar_and_event_club_in_former_sgt_pepper_space_with_pizza_live_bands_djs_salsa_student_nights_pride_afterparties_casual_door_and_event_led_queer_presence',
      'identity_note', 'Club Tai Pan operates at 194 Long Street in the former SGT Pepper space. The stored sgtpepperct.com link represents the previous venue identity and should be replaced by the current Club Tai Pan social channel.',
